#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-compact [WHAT TO KEEP]

Asks for this conversation to be compacted when the current turn ends: for the main session of a contained
Claude session, once the compaction offer has come (past compact_offer tokens). WHAT TO KEEP goes to the summary
along with fixed instructions. After the compaction you are prompted to continue.

This command only states the wish and prints that nothing is scheduled. The compaction mod (DEVELOPMENT.md
§5.12) sees the Bash call, refuses it in a subagent and below the offer's size, and otherwise puts "compaction
is scheduled" in that line's place. So a call it can't see (inside a script, `bash -c`, a function) says the
truth by itself.
"""
import sys

if sys.argv[1:2] in (["-h"], ["--help"]):
    print(__doc__.strip())
    sys.exit(0)
keep = " ".join(" ".join(sys.argv[1:]).split())     # one line: the mod reads to its end
# the mod replaces this line (UNSEEN in sandbox/mods/compaction/hooks/register.ts)
print("cc-compact: nothing scheduled: containedclaude did not see this call. Run cc-compact as a command of its "
      "own (not inside a script or bash -c).")
if keep:
    print("Keep: " + keep)          # the mod reads it from here (KEEP in register.ts)
